Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:03:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ramboot: auto-select preferred GOP mode

Series note (Remy, root, 2026-10-31): the op6/e1-demo bootloader fork already carries this change as 41317dc (whose subject this patch now carries) plus follow-up 55ded92. The original subject matched nothing in the fork's log, so integrate.sh's subject-based skip missed it, git am stopped on the already-present change, and 0003/0004 were silently never applied (R-1 attempt 1 root cause). Subject aligned to the fork's; patch content unchanged.

Agent: Codex root
Model: gpt-6-sol
Provider: OpenAI
Refs: perplexity-redox-hourly-safety-check
---
 src/main.rs | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.rs b/src/main.rs
index 0b4ee2b..6ce5acc 100644
--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -160,6 +160,12 @@ fn select_mode(
     }
     println!();
 
+    // RAM boot must reach the kernel without a working firmware keyboard.
+    // Keep the preferred/current resolution (or largest-mode fallback) above.
+    if cfg!(feature = "ramboot") {
+        return modes.iter().find(|(mode, _)| mode.id == selected).map(|(mode, _)| *mode);
+    }
+
     println!("Arrow keys and enter select mode");
     #[cfg(not(feature = "ramboot"))]
     let live_mode = os.get_text_position();
